   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Cubs In Five** (1 review): This is the earliest concert in which Cubs In Five appears [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Night of the Mules**: rare: 6 archived performances [4]\n- **Going to Reykjavik**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **West Country Dream**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 10 archived performances [4]\n- **Going to Scotland**: rare: 12 archived performances [4]\n- **Masher**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 8 archived performances [4]\n- **Cold Milk Bottle**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Song For the Julian Calendar**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 9 archived performances [4]\n- **Sept 19th Triple X Love Love**: rare: 7 archived performances [4]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: Cubs In Five [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **MountainGoats1997-06-17.SBD** (recommended): soundboard; 21 songs; 59 min; rated 4.5/5 by 2 [1]. Said about its sound: Described as a solid soundboard recording; The audience is very audible and the stereo imaging is clear [2][3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- There is little stage banter, but the song selection is good [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **MountainGoats1997-06-17.SBD**: taped by unknown; source: SBD>DAT [1]. Also: Reviewer doubts the source is purely soundboard, given the audience presence and stereo image, and asks for background on it [3]",
